searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"MedFabric.Domain","doc":"Pure encounter decisions within Med Fabric.","ref":"MedFabric.Domain.html"},{"type":"module","title":"MedFabric.Domain.Encounter","doc":"Clinical recording intake and review rules.","ref":"MedFabric.Domain.Encounter.html"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Domain.Encounter.metadata/3","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Domain.Encounter.html#metadata/3"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Domain.Encounter.review/3","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Domain.Encounter.html#review/3"},{"type":"module","title":"MedFabric.Interop","doc":"Healthcare record exchange within Med Fabric.","ref":"MedFabric.Interop.html"},{"type":"module","title":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient","doc":"Exports a reviewed recording to FHIR R4 using conditional create by identifier.\n\nThe test server receives synthetic clinical references. Fixture origin and\ncontinuity describe the reviewed artifact independently of those references.","ref":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient.html"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient.build_observation/4","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient.html#build_observation/4"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient.deliver/2","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient.html#deliver/2"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient.fetch_by_identifier/2","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient.html#fetch_by_identifier/2"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient.seed_exam/2","doc":"Seeds a synthetic patient and encounter using stable identifiers on the receiving server.","ref":"MedFabric.Interop.FhirClient.html#seed_exam/2"},{"type":"module","title":"MedFabric.Store","doc":"Clinical persistence and audit within Med Fabric.","ref":"MedFabric.Store.html"},{"type":"module","title":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres","doc":"Atomic recording intake, review and manual export.","ref":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.html"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.accept/5","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.html#accept/5"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.bytes/2","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.html#bytes/2"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.child_spec/1","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.delivery_result/3","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.html#delivery_result/3"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.fetch/2","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.html#fetch/2"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.migrate/1","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.html#migrate/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.ready/6","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.html#ready/6"},{"type":"function","title":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.start_link/1","doc":"","ref":"MedFabric.Store.Postgres.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"extras","title":"Med Fabric changelog","doc":"# Med Fabric changelog","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Unreleased - Med Fabric changelog","doc":"- Established the initial workspace boundary and architecture plan.","ref":"changelog.html#unreleased"},{"type":"extras","title":"LICENSE","doc":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 nshkrdotcom\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.","ref":"license.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"README","doc":"Med Fabric \n\n \n     \n     \n \n\n`Med Fabric` is an Elixir poncho for durable remote clinical encounters, atomic clinician observation acceptance, and HL7 FHIR R4 delivery. The exam uses one Welded `:med_ex` SDK for WebRTC preview and recording.\n\n---","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Projects - README","doc":"| Path | Responsibility |\n| --- | --- |\n| [core/domain](core/domain/README.md) | Bind acquisition facts and decide explicit acceptance in pure Elixir |\n| [core/store](core/store/README.md) | Commit acceptance, provenance, and outbox in one PostgreSQL transaction |\n| [core/interop](core/interop/README.md) | Deliver and confirm one reviewed observation over FHIR R4 |\n| [apps/exam](apps/exam/README.md) | Boot Phoenix, authorize the lab, and host the review and delivery UI |\n\nFollow the [native browser-to-record runbook](docs/architecture/browser-to-record.md) for Ubuntu 26.04 onboarding, diagrams, focused tests, and the listening check.","ref":"readme.html#projects"},{"type":"extras","title":"Native browser-to-record lab","doc":"# Native browser-to-record lab\n\nThis lab associates a versioned PhysioNet fixture with a synthetic encounter in an explicitly enabled localhost app. MedEx provides capture, Opus RTP, and the browser hook. Med Fabric owns the encounter, PostgreSQL commit, and FHIR delivery.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  Browser[\"Clinician browser\"] <-->|\"Authenticated signaling and RTP\"| Exam[\"Exam and pinned MedEx SDK\"]\n  WAV[\"Verified CirCor fixture\"] --> Exam\n  Exam --> Artifact[\"Immutable WAV by full-file digest\"]\n  Artifact -->|\"Ready metadata + PCM digest\"| PG\n  Browser -->|\"Review and accept\"| Exam\n  Exam -->|\"One commit\"| PG[\"PostgreSQL ready recording, acceptance and outbox\"]\n  PG --> Export[\"Confirm delivery\"]\n  Export -->|\"Conditional create + read-back\"| HAPI[\"Native HAPI FHIR R4\"]\n```\n\nThe exam supervisor starts PubSub, Postgrex, a capture runner, and the Phoenix endpoint. The channel owns its peer. The capture task owns acquisition completion, with a bounded best-effort preview worker. The runner holds only the active task and its last failure. The SDK installs immutable WAVs by complete-file hash and returns a separate PCM digest. PostgreSQL owns ready metadata, conflicting evidence, reviewer identity and the export row. Review fetches and verifies the bytes before acceptance. Delivery uses seeded synthetic references and manual retry. Keep the artifact directory and service state across restarts.","ref":"browser-to-record.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Setup on Ubuntu 26.04 - Native browser-to-record lab","doc":"1. Install `git curl tar build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev ca-certificates jq openssl postgresql-18 postgresql-client-18`. Use a non-root account for the isolated PostgreSQL cluster. Have `uv` on PATH. Network access and authenticated access to the private SDK repo are required on a fresh clone.\n2. With asdf or mise, activate the Erlang and Elixir versions in `.tool-versions` and Node `24.19.0`. For native HAPI, choose Temurin `21.0.9+10` and activate a full JDK. For example, `mise install java@temurin-21.0.9+10` and `export JAVA_HOME=\"$(mise where java@temurin-21.0.9+10)\"`. The HAPI build pins and checksums the upstream source and Maven distribution.\n3. Run `./onboard.sh --integration` from Fabric. The browser installation needs Chromium host libraries. If missing, run `ops/browser/node_modules/.bin/playwright install-deps chromium` with appropriate system privileges and retry. `./onboard.sh` alone prepares ordinary Mix checks.\n4. Run `ops/verify_browser.sh`. It starts disposable local PostgreSQL 18 and JVM HAPI if service URLs are absent. To reuse dedicated test services, export both `DATABASE_URL` and `FHIR_BASE_URL`; they must be safe for synthetic test data. Service ports default to 15432 and 18080, with `MF_POSTGRES_PORT` and `MF_HAPI_PORT` overrides. `MF_HTTP_PORT` defaults to 14000. It prepares the pinned SDK's fixture, starts the normal exam process, proves real browser audio before and after preview replacement, verifies the artifact hash, restarts the exam before acceptance, verifies the recovered WAV, delivers once, then restarts the exam and its owned file-backed HAPI receiver for independent read-back. It records its run directory under `_build`. Use `ops/verify_browser.sh --release` to exercise the assembled Mix release through the same browser check.","ref":"browser-to-record.html#setup-on-ubuntu-26-04"},{"type":"extras","title":"Focused checks - Native browser-to-record lab","doc":"- `cd core/domain && mix test` checks the reviewed file identity and conflict gate.\n- `cd core/store && mix test integration` exercises PostgreSQL rollback, concurrent duplicates, reconnect, and delivery state. Set `DATABASE_URL` first.\n- `cd core/interop && mix test integration` proves one real HAPI resource after the response to an accepted write is discarded. Set `FHIR_BASE_URL` first.\n- `mix test`, `mix quality`, and `mix weld.verify` from the root cover ordinary child checks and the library projection. The browser runner exercises the actual exam path.","ref":"browser-to-record.html#focused-checks"},{"type":"extras","title":"Manual listening check - Native browser-to-record lab","doc":"1. Export `JAVA_HOME` and run `native_env=$(ops/local_services.sh start) && eval \"$native_env\"`. Prepare data with `bash apps/exam/deps/med_ex/priv/fixtures/prepare.sh \"$PWD/_build/circor\"`.\n2. In the root shell export `MF_LAB=1`, `MF_EXAM_ID=manual-$(openssl rand -hex 8)`, `MF_LAB_ACCESS_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 24)`, `MF_SECRET_KEY_BASE=$(openssl rand -hex 48)`, `MF_FIXTURE_DIR=$PWD/_build/circor`, and `MF_ARTIFACT_DIR=$PWD/_build/manual-recordings`. Set `export MF_REFS_FILE=$MF_ARTIFACT_DIR/$MF_EXAM_ID-refs.json`. Run `mkdir -p \"$MF_ARTIFACT_DIR\" && (cd apps/exam && env -u MF_LAB mix run --no-start ../../ops/seed_exam.exs) && (cd apps/exam && mix run --no-halt)`.\n3. Open `http://127.0.0.1:4000/encounters/$MF_EXAM_ID?key=$MF_LAB_ACCESS_KEY` with the variable values substituted. Select **Play preview**, then **Start capture**. Listen for the fixture, disconnect preview, and reconnect before capture finishes. Listen for audio after reconnect. Capture should remain active across preview loss.\n4. Play the finalized recording and verify its displayed continuity. Select **Accept recording**, refresh, and select **Deliver to FHIR**. Check the read-back count and recording digest with the automated runner or an identifier search on the test server. Record the browser version, whether audio was audible, encounter ID, and remote reference.\n5. Stop the exam process and run `ops/local_services.sh stop` for the local services you started.","ref":"browser-to-record.html#manual-listening-check"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.5"}}